course: dictionary
lesson: 13313
title: Grille: a metal screen
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A grille is a grid or screen made of metal bars or wires. It covers a window, a door, an opening or a vent. «The shop window had a metal grille to keep thieves out.» The grille protects the window, and you can still see through it.
explain: A grille can also let air or sound pass through while keeping things out. «The air vent in the classroom had a grille, so fresh air could flow in.» Look for grilles on drains, speakers and vents the next time you are out.
explain: A car has a grille too. It is the metal grid at the front that lets air reach the engine. «The car's grille was covered in bugs after the long drive.» The context tells you the grille is part of the car, not a window.
explain: Safety first: never poke your fingers or a stick through a grille. The bars are there to protect you and the thing behind them.
fact: A grille is a grid or screen made of metal bars or wires.
fact: «Grille» means a metal grid across a window, door, opening or vent, to protect it or let air through.
fact: On a car, the grille is the metal grid at the front that lets air reach the engine.
fact: In old buildings, a small grille in a door lets people look or talk through it before they open it.
fact: Grille is a noun: one grille, many grilles.
exercise: «The shop window had a metal grille to keep thieves out.» What is the grille for? | To carry water up to the roof | To play music for shoppers | *To protect the window from thieves | To make the window turn pink
exercise: Dad points to the front of the car: «Look at the grille.» What is a car's grille? | The seat where the driver sits | *The metal grid at the front that lets air reach the engine | The horn that beeps | The wheel that turns the car
exercise: «The air vent in the classroom had a grille.» Find and copy the word that means a metal screen over an opening. | classroom | vent | fresh | *grille
test: Which word means a grid or screen of metal bars across an opening? | carpet | pillow | *grille | ladder
test: «The old door had a small grille, so people could look through it before they opened the door.» What did the grille let people do? | Paint the door | *Look or talk through it before opening the door | Open the door faster | Hide inside the door
exam: «Why must you never poke your fingers through a grille?» | Because grilles always move | Because grilles are made of soft wood | Because grilles are too small to see | *Because you could get hurt
